      "id": 1,
      "text": "Norway began as Mount Walleston in 1845, founded by Norwegian immigrant Hans Erasmus Hiorth who built the county’s first sawmill on the Tippecanoe River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        27,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/norway_indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name changed to Norway to honor its founders’ Norwegian roots, a nod to the many settlers from Norway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        4,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norway%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office opened on January 14, 1898, and closed less than a year later on December 30, 1899.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/norway_indiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "John Armstrong’s 1845 plat mapped 96 lots, naming streets after figures such as Hiorth, Washington, and Franklin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/norway_indiana",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Norway lies just below the Norway Dam on the Tippecanoe River, which creates Lake Shafer that hosts Indiana Beach amusement park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norway%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The early mills powered by the dam supplied lumber for Monticello and other early structures, making Norway an initial industrial hub in White County.",
